* `output`: the output image as a 2D array of float values
* `kernel`: the Gaussian kernel coefficients as a 1D array of float values
* `size`: the image size as an `int2` value
* `sigma`: the Gaussian blur sigma as a float value

The kernel iterates over the Gaussian kernel and samples the input image at each offset position, accumulating the contributions of each kernel sample. The output pixel value is then normalized by the sum of the kernel weights.

