$queue = new SplQueue();

function executeJob()
{
    global $queue;

    // Get a job from the queue
    if (!$queue->count()) {
        echo "Queue is empty\n";
        return;
    }

    // Execute the job
    echo "Executing job\n";
    // Your job execution code here
    sleep(2);
    echo "Job finished\n";

    // Remove the job from the queue
    $queue->dequeue();
}

// Create a worker pool
$workers = [];
for ($i = 0; $i < $maxRunning; $i++) {
    $worker = new class($executeJob) extends Coroutine {
        private function $executeJob;

        public function __construct($executeJob)
        {
            parent::__construct();
            $this->executeJob = $executeJob;
        }

        public function start()
        {
            parent::start();
            while (true) {
                $queue->safe($this->executeJob);
            }
        }
    };
    $worker->start();
}

// Add jobs to the queue
for ($i = 0; $i < 10; $i++) {
    $queue->enqueue(new class() extends Coroutine {
        public function start()
        {
            parent::start();
            echo "Job added to queue\n";
        }
    });
}
```

In this example, we create a worker pool with the maximum running coroutines (5) and use a queue to send jobs to the workers. When a worker finishes executing a job, it gets another job from the queue and executes it. If the queue is empty, the worker waits for a job to be added to the queue.

