1. Install npcap:
Download and install npcap from its official website (<https://npcap.org/>). npcap is a packet capture driver that allows you to access network traffic on Windows systems.

2. Choose a programming language:
Select a programming language you're comfortable with and that supports Windows service development. C# and C++ are good choices.

3. Create a new Windows Service project:
Use your preferred IDE (Integrated Development Environment) to create a new Windows Service project in the chosen language.

4. Include required libraries:
Add the necessary libraries for packet capture and decoding. If you're using C++, you might want to use Pcap (<https://github.com/pcapdotnet/pcap>) or WinPcap (<https://www.winpcap.org/>) to interact with npcap. If you're using C#, consider using NPcap.Net (<https://github.com/nate-car/NPcap.Net>) or Pcap.Net (<https://pcapdotnet.codeplex.com/>).

5. Write the service logic:
In the service's main logic, initialize the packet capture and create a loop to capture, decode, and process packets.

Here is a basic outline of the service logic in C++, using Pcap:

```cpp
#include <pcap.h>
// ... other includes ...

void processPacket(const u_char *packet, const struct pcap_pkthdr *header) {
    // Decode and process the packet here
}

int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
    // Initialize npcap
    char errbuf[PCAP_ERRBUF_SIZE];
    pcap_if_t* devices;

    if (pcap_findalldevs(&devices, errbuf) == -1) {
        // Handle error
    }

    // Choose the device you want to capture on
    pcap_t* handle = pcap_open_live(devices->name, 65536, 1, 1000, errbuf);

    if (handle == NULL) {
        // Handle error
    }

    // Set the filter (e.g., to capture only TCP traffic)
    bpf_program filter;
    char filter_exp[] = "tcp";

    if (pcap_compile(handle, &filter, filter_exp, 0, 0) == -1) {
        // Handle error
    }

    if (pcap_setfilter(handle, &filter) == -1) {
        // Handle error
    }

    // Start capturing packets
    while (true) {
        u_char packet[65536];
        struct pcap_pkthdr header;

        int packet_received = pcap_next_ex(handle, &header, (const u_char**)&packet);

        if (packet_received == -1) {
            // Handle error
        }

        if (packet_received == 0) {
            // Timed out, continue the loop
            continue;
        }

        processPacket(packet, &header);
    }

    // Clean up
    pcap_freecode(&filter);
    pcap_close(handle);
    pcap_freealldevs(devices);

    return 0;
}
```

